# Tea Time — Privacy Policy

**Effective date:** October 13, 2026

Tea Time (“the App”) is a personal journaling application that helps users write journal entries, track moods, organize journals, and personalize entries with stickers and other features.

This Privacy Policy explains how information is handled when you use Tea Time.

## 1. Information You Enter

Tea Time may let you create and store:
- Journal entries, notes, and journal titles
- Mood check-ins and related history
- To-do lists, sleep records, and achievements
- Favorites, stickers, and personalization settings

Your journal entries may contain sensitive personal information. Please avoid entering information you do not want stored on your device or exposed to anyone who can access your device.

## 2. How Your Information Is Stored

Tea Time uses the storage mechanisms implemented in the installed version of the App. Some journal information and preferences may be stored locally on your device.

Uninstalling the App, clearing its data, or losing your device may result in the loss of locally stored information.

Unless a specific backup or synchronization feature is provided and explained within the App, do not assume your journal entries are backed up or synchronized across devices.

## 3. Device Security

Tea Time may offer a PIN or biometric-lock feature. These features are intended to help restrict access to the App.

Biometric authentication is handled through supported Android device authentication facilities. Tea Time does not need to receive your fingerprint or face data to request authentication.

An in-app lock should not be treated as a guarantee of encryption or complete protection against unauthorized access to device data.

## 4. Permissions and Updates

Tea Time may request Android permissions when needed for optional features. The purpose of each permission should be explained when the feature is used.

The App may use Google Play services to check for and install available app updates when distributed through Google Play. Google Play handles its own data processing under Google's applicable privacy terms.

## 5. Sharing and Selling Information

We do not sell your personal journal entries.

The information shared with external services, if any, depends on the features and third-party software included in the version you use. This policy should be updated if analytics, advertising, cloud synchronization, crash reporting, or other services collect or transmit information.

## 6. Data Retention and Deletion

Information stored locally may remain on your device until you delete it, clear the App's data, or uninstall the App. The exact behavior depends on the storage method used by the installed version.

If a future version provides online storage or account-based features, the applicable retention and deletion process will be explained in an updated policy.

## 7. Children's Privacy

Tea Time is not intended to collect personal information from children in violation of applicable law. If you believe information has been collected inappropriately, please contact us using the address below.

## 8. Security

We take reasonable steps appropriate to the App's design to protect information. However, no method of storage or transmission can be guaranteed to be completely secure. Users should keep their devices updated and protected.

## 9. Changes to This Policy

This Privacy Policy may be updated when the App's features, data practices, or legal requirements change. The latest version should be made available at the public privacy-policy URL listed in Google Play.

